# RF Games Platform

## Ownership
You are the design + technical lead. Decide UI system details, naming (except when user locks a name), architecture, and polish. Ask only when a product rule is ambiguous.

## Monorepo
- `shared/` — pure game logic, types, bots, orchestrators (no DOM)
- `client/` — React UI, canvas, hooks
- `server/` — rooms, Socket.io, validation
- After shared changes: `npm run build:shared`
- PowerShell: use `;` not `&&` when chaining fails

## Multi-game hub
- Home picks a game; do not bury Game 2 inside Kare Kapmaca lobby
- Shared chrome (header leave-home, parchment language) may be reused; each game may have its own accent/personality
- Online namespaces/events must be game-scoped (`room:` for Kapmaca is fine; Game 2 uses distinct events or `gameId`)

## Quality bar
- Contrast: idle tabs/buttons must stay readable on parchment
- Touch + mouse + pen for canvas games
- Local bots where it makes sense (Kapmaca yes; fold-draw no AI artist unless asked)
- Prefer real interaction over decorative cards
- Verify with browser or Playwright after meaningful UI/game changes

## Forbidden
- Breaking Kapmaca rules while building Game 2
- Committing without explicit ask
- CORS `*` in production advice without warning

## Skills
Apply project skills in `.cursor/skills/` and relevant user skills (`frontend-design`, `develop-web-game`, `react-best-practices`, `webapp-testing`, `security-best-practices`).
